<title>UK: EBRD names vp for evaluation, nuclear safety.</title>
<headline>EBRD names vp for evaluation, nuclear safety.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development said on Thursday Joachim Jahnke had been apointed vice-president for project evaluation, operations support and nuclear safety.</p>
<p>Jahnke, 57, worked for the German government and the European Commission before joining the EBRD in 1993.</p>
<p>His responsibilities include procurement and consultants, official co-financing, the Nuclear Safety Account, functional responsibiility for energy matters and project evaluation.</p>
<p>He succeeds Manfred Abelein who retired at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Thatcher, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770</p>
